{"id":"cb98a9051c85002229c3648087afdd0006bf4a8f","axis":"silent","repo":"envoyproxy/envoy","sha":"cb98a9051c85002229c3648087afdd0006bf4a8f","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"api/envoy/config/route/v3/route_components.proto","lines":["@@ -895,7 +895,7 @@ message RouteAction {","   // .. note::","   //","   //   Shadowing doesn't support HTTP CONNECT and upgrades.","-  // [#next-free-field: 9]","+  // [#next-free-field: 10]","   message RequestMirrorPolicy {","     option (udpa.annotations.versioning).previous_message_type =","         \"envoy.api.v2.route.RouteAction.RequestMirrorPolicy\";","@@ -963,6 +963,20 @@ message RouteAction {","     // is implicitly enabled if this field is set.","     string host_rewrite_literal = 8","         [(validate.rules).string = {well_known_regex: HTTP_HEADER_VALUE strict: false}];","+","+    // The human readable prefix to use when emitting statistics for this mirror policy. The","+    // statistics are rooted at ``mirror.<stat_prefix>.`` and count how many requests were","+    // selected for mirroring, how many mirrors were started, and how each mirror ended. See","+    // :ref:`mirror policy statistics <config_http_filters_router_mirror_stats>`.","+    //","+    // The statistics are emitted in the server's root scope, so policies that use the same","+    // ``stat_prefix`` share the same counters, wherever they are configured. This includes","+    // cluster-level :ref:`request_mirror_policies","+    // <envoy_v3_api_field_extensions.upstreams.http.v3.HttpProtocolOptions.request_mirror_policies>`,","+    // which take precedence over route-level policies.","+    //","+    // If empty, no per policy statistics are emitted.","+    string stat_prefix = 9;","   }"," ","   // Specifies the route's hashing policy if the upstream cluster uses a hashing :ref:`load balancer"],"additions":15,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"changelogs/current/new_features/router__mirror-policy-stats.rst","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,6 @@","+Added :ref:`stat_prefix <envoy_v3_api_field_config.route.v3.RouteAction.RequestMirrorPolicy.stat_prefix>`","+to request mirror policies, at route, virtual host, route configuration and cluster level. When","+set, the router emits per policy counters rooted at ``mirror.<stat_prefix>.`` for mirrors selected","+by the runtime fraction, mirrors skipped because the mirror cluster is missing, mirrors started,","+and mirrors that ended with a 2xx response, with a failure or non-2xx response, or were cancelled.","+See :ref:`mirror policy statistics <config_http_filters_router_mirror_stats>`."],"additions":6,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"docs/root/configuration/http/http_filters/router_filter.rst","lines":["@@ -478,6 +478,43 @@ statistics:","    they are counted in ``cluster.<name>.retry.upstream_rq_<*>`` instead. See","    :ref:`cluster retry statistics <config_cluster_manager_cluster_stats_retry>` for details."," ","+.. _config_http_filters_router_mirror_stats:","+","+Mirror policies","+^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^","+","+A :ref:`request mirror policy <envoy_v3_api_msg_config.route.v3.RouteAction.RequestMirrorPolicy>`","+with a :ref:`stat_prefix","+<envoy_v3_api_field_config.route.v3.RouteAction.RequestMirrorPolicy.stat_prefix>` outputs","+statistics in the ``mirror.<stat_prefix>.`` namespace:","+","+.. csv-table::","+  :header: Name, Type, Description","+  :widths: 1, 1, 2","+","+  rq_sampled, Counter, Total requests selected for mirroring by the policy runtime fraction","+  rq_no_cluster, Counter, Total selected requests not mirrored because the mirror cluster did not exist or the cluster header was missing","+  rq_started, Counter, Total mirror requests started","+  rq_success, Counter, Total mirror requests that received a 2xx response","+  rq_failure, Counter, Total mirror requests that received a non-2xx response or failed without a response","+  rq_cancelled, Counter, Total mirror requests cancelled because the primary request was destroyed before the request was fully sent","+","+The statistics are emitted in the server's root scope and tagged with the policy ``stat_prefix``.","+Policies that use the same ``stat_prefix`` share the same counters, including policies of different","+routes, virtual hosts or route configurations. Cluster-level :ref:`request_mirror_policies","+<envoy_v3_api_field_extensions.upstreams.http.v3.HttpProtocolOptions.request_mirror_policies>`","+emit the same statistics. When a cluster has mirror policies, they replace the route-level","+policies, so only the statistics of the cluster-level policies are updated.","+","+Mirror policies are evaluated once the router has selected an upstream host for the primary","+request. Requests answered locally before that point, for example because the cluster has no","+healthy upstream or because the request is load shed, are not counted in ``rq_sampled``, and","+neither are CONNECT requests, which are never mirrored. ``rq_sampled`` minus ``rq_no_cluster``","+minus ``rq_started`` counts the selected requests that were not mirrored because an upstream HTTP","+filter answered the primary request locally after the policies were evaluated.","+``rq_started`` minus ``rq_success``, ``rq_failure`` and ``rq_cancelled`` counts the mirror requests","+still in flight.","+"," Runtime"," -------"," "],"additions":37,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"envoy/router/BUILD","lines":["@@ -94,6 +94,7 @@ envoy_cc_library(","         \"//envoy/http:header_evaluator\",","         \"//envoy/http:header_map_interface\",","         \"//envoy/rds:rds_config_interface\",","+        \"//envoy/stats:stats_macros\",","         \"//envoy/stream_info:stream_info_interface\",","         \"//envoy/tcp:conn_pool_interface\",","         \"//envoy/tracing:tracer_interface\","],"additions":1,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"envoy/router/router.h","lines":["@@ -24,6 +24,7 @@"," #include \"envoy/router/path_matcher.h\""," #include \"envoy/router/path_rewriter.h\""," #include \"envoy/router/retry.h\"","+#include \"envoy/stats/stats_macros.h\""," #include \"envoy/stream_info/stream_info.h\""," #include \"envoy/tcp/conn_pool.h\""," #include \"envoy/tracing/tracer.h\"","@@ -245,6 +246,26 @@ class InternalRedirectPolicy {","   virtual bool isCrossSchemeRedirectAllowed() const PURE;"," };"," ","+/**","+ * All mirror policy stats. @see stats_macro.h","+ */","+#define ALL_SHADOW_POLICY_STATS(COUNTER)                                                           \\","+  COUNTER(rq_cancelled)                                                                            \\","+  COUNTER(rq_failure)                                                                              \\","+  COUNTER(rq_no_cluster)                                                                           \\","+  COUNTER(rq_sampled)                                                                              \\","+  COUNTER(rq_started)                                                                              \\","+  COUNTER(rq_success)","+","+/**","+ * Struct definition for all mirror policy stats. @see stats_macro.h","+ */","+struct ShadowPolicyStats {","+  ALL_SHADOW_POLICY_STATS(GENERATE_COUNTER_STRUCT)","+};","+","+using ShadowPolicyStatsSharedPtr = std::shared_ptr<const ShadowPolicyStats>;","+"," /**","  * Per route policy for request shadowing.","  */","@@ -299,6 +320,13 @@ class ShadowPolicy {","    * @return the literal value to rewrite the host header with, or empty if no rewrite.","    */","   virtual absl::string_view hostRewriteLiteral() const PURE;","+","+  /**","+   * @return the stats of this policy, or nullptr if the policy has no stat prefix. The returned","+   *         pointer keeps the stats alive, so it can be held by a mirror request that outlives","+   *         the route configuration.","+   */","+  virtual const ShadowPolicyStatsSharedPtr& stats() const PURE;"," };"," "," using ShadowPolicyPtr = std::shared_ptr<ShadowPolicy>;"],"additions":28,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"envoy/router/shadow_writer.h","lines":["@@ -10,6 +10,9 @@"," namespace Envoy {"," namespace Router {"," ","+struct ShadowPolicyStats;","+using ShadowPolicyStatsSharedPtr = std::shared_ptr<const ShadowPolicyStats>;","+"," /**","  * Interface used to shadow complete requests to an alternate upstream cluster in a \"fire and","  * forget\" fashion. Right now this interface takes a fully buffered request and cannot be used for","@@ -24,9 +27,11 @@ class ShadowWriter {","    * @param cluster supplies the cluster name to shadow to.","    * @param message supplies the complete request to shadow.","    * @param options supplies the request options for the underlying asynchronous request.","+   * @param stats supplies the stats of the mirror policy, or nullptr if it has none.","    */","   virtual void shadow(const std::string& cluster, Http::RequestMessagePtr&& request,","-                      const Http::AsyncClient::RequestOptions& options) PURE;","+                      const Http::AsyncClient::RequestOptions& options,","+                      const ShadowPolicyStatsSharedPtr& stats) PURE;"," ","   /**","    * Initialize shadowing a request. Differs from the above in that additional","@@ -34,13 +39,15 @@ class ShadowWriter {","    * @param cluster supplies the cluster name to shadow to.","    * @param headers supplies the headers for initializing the shadow.","    * @param options supplies the request options for the underlying asynchronous request.","+   * @param stats supplies the stats of the mirror policy, or nullptr if it has none.","    * @return OngoingRequest* pointer owned by the AsyncClient which can have additional data and","    *                         trailers sent to it. Can be null if the stream is immediately","    *                         cancelled.","    */","   virtual Http::AsyncClient::OngoingRequest*","   streamingShadow(const std::string& cluster, Http::RequestHeaderMapPtr&& headers,","-                  const Http::AsyncClient::RequestOptions& options) PURE;","+                  const Http::AsyncClient::RequestOptions& options,","+                  const ShadowPolicyStatsSharedPtr& stats) PURE;"," };"," "," using ShadowWriterPtr = std::unique_ptr<ShadowWriter>;"],"additions":9,"deletions":2,"truncated":false},{"path":"source/common/config/well_known_names.cc","lines":["@@ -224,6 +224,10 @@ TagNameValues::TagNameValues() {","   // connection_limit.(<stat_prefix>.)*","   addTokenized(CONNECTION_LIMIT_PREFIX, \"connection_limit.$.**\");"," ","+  // mirror.(<stat_prefix>.)rq_<stat>","+  // Note: <stat_prefix> can contain dots, so everything up to the final rq_ stat is extracted.","+  addRe2(MIRROR_PREFIX, R\"(^mirror\\.((.+)\\.)rq_\\w+$)\", \"mirror.\");","+","   // [http.|cluster.]<stat_prefix>.rbac.[<optional rules stat_prefix>.]policy.(<policy","   // name>.).(allowed|shadow_allowed|denied|shadow_denied)","   addRe2("],"additions":4,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"source/common/config/well_known_names.h","lines":["@@ -133,6 +133,8 @@ class TagNameValues {","   const std::string DNS_FILTER_PREFIX = \"envoy.dns_filter_prefix\";","   // Stats prefix for the Connection limit filter","   const std::string CONNECTION_LIMIT_PREFIX = \"envoy.connection_limit_prefix\";","+  // Stats prefix for a request mirror policy","+  const std::string MIRROR_PREFIX = \"envoy.mirror_prefix\";","   // Stats prefix for the RBAC network filter","   const std::string RBAC_PREFIX = \"envoy.rbac_prefix\";","   // Rules/shadow rules stats prefix for the RBAC network filter"],"additions":2,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"source/common/router/BUILD","lines":["@@ -540,11 +540,16 @@ envoy_cc_library(","     srcs = [\"shadow_writer_impl.cc\"],","     hdrs = [\"shadow_writer_impl.h\"],","     deps = [","+        \"//envoy/event:deferred_deletable\",","+        \"//envoy/event:dispatcher_interface\",","+        \"//envoy/router:router_interface\",","         \"//envoy/router:shadow_writer_interface\",","         \"//envoy/upstream:cluster_manager_interface\",","         \"//source/common/common:assert_lib\",","+        \"//source/common/http:codes_lib\",","         \"//source/common/http:header_utility_lib\",","         \"//source/common/http:headers_lib\",","+        \"//source/common/http:utility_lib\",","     ],"," )"," "],"additions":5,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"source/common/router/config_impl.cc","lines":["@@ -410,8 +410,23 @@ ShadowPolicyImpl::ShadowPolicyImpl(const RequestMirrorPolicy& config,","     SET_AND_RETURN_IF_NOT_OK(mutations_or_error.status(), creation_status);","     request_headers_mutations_ = std::move(mutations_or_error.value());","   }","+","+  if (!config.stat_prefix().empty()) {","+    // mirror.(<stat_prefix>.)*","+    auto holder =","+        std::make_shared<ShadowPolicyStatsHolder>(factory_context.scope().createScopeWithTaggedName(","+            \"mirror\",","+            {Stats::TagStringView{Envoy::Config::TagNames::get().MIRROR_PREFIX,","+                                  config.stat_prefix()}},","+            absl::StrCat(\"mirror.\", config.stat_prefix())));","+    // Share ownership with the holder so that the scope outlives in-flight mirror requests.","+    stats_ = ShadowPolicyStatsSharedPtr(holder, &holder->stats_);","+  }"," }"," ","+ShadowPolicyImpl::ShadowPolicyStatsHolder::ShadowPolicyStatsHolder(Stats::ScopeSharedPtr scope)","+    : scope_(std::move(scope)), stats_{ALL_SHADOW_POLICY_STATS(POOL_COUNTER(*scope_))} {}","+"," const Http::HeaderEvaluator& ShadowPolicyImpl::headerEvaluator() const {","   if (request_headers_mutations_) {","     return *request_headers_mutations_;"],"additions":15,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"source/common/router/config_impl.h","lines":["@@ -575,8 +575,16 @@ class ShadowPolicyImpl : public ShadowPolicy {","   }","   const Http::HeaderEvaluator& headerEvaluator() const override;","   absl::string_view hostRewriteLiteral() const override { return host_rewrite_literal_; }","+  const ShadowPolicyStatsSharedPtr& stats() const override { return stats_; }"," "," private:","+  struct ShadowPolicyStatsHolder {","+    explicit ShadowPolicyStatsHolder(Stats::ScopeSharedPtr scope);","+","+    const Stats::ScopeSharedPtr scope_;","+    const ShadowPolicyStats stats_;","+  };","+","   explicit ShadowPolicyImpl(const RequestMirrorPolicy& config,","                             Server::Configuration::CommonFactoryContext& factory_context,","                             absl::Status& creation_status);","@@ -589,6 +597,7 @@ class ShadowPolicyImpl : public ShadowPolicy {","   const bool disable_shadow_host_suffix_append_;","   const std::string host_rewrite_literal_;","   HeaderMutationsPtr request_headers_mutations_;","+  ShadowPolicyStatsSharedPtr stats_;"," };"," "," /**"],"additions":9,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"source/common/router/router.cc","lines":["@@ -872,7 +872,8 @@ bool Filter::continueDecodeHeaders(Http::RequestHeaderMap& headers, bool end_str","   absl::InlinedVector<std::reference_wrapper<const ShadowPolicy>, 2> active_shadow_policies;"," ","   // Determine which shadow policies to use. It's possible that we don't do any shadowing due to","-  // runtime keys. Also the method CONNECT doesn't support shadowing.","+  // runtime keys. Also the method CONNECT doesn't support shadowing. Requests answered locally","+  // before host selection never get here, so they are not counted in rq_sampled.","   const absl::string_view method = headers.getMethodValue();","   if (method != Http::Headers::get().MethodValues.Connect) {","     // Use cluster-level shadow policies if they are available (most specific wins).","@@ -885,6 +886,9 @@ bool Filter::continueDecodeHeaders(Http::RequestHeaderMap& headers, bool end_str","       const auto& policy_ref = *shadow_policy;","       if (FilterUtility::shouldShadow(policy_ref, config_->runtime_, callbacks_->streamId())) {","         active_shadow_policies.push_back(std::cref(policy_ref));","+        if (policy_ref.stats() != nullptr) {","+          policy_ref.stats()->rq_sampled_.inc();","+        }","       }","     }","   }","@@ -940,6 +944,9 @@ bool Filter::continueDecodeHeaders(Http::RequestHeaderMap& headers, bool end_str","     const std::optional<absl::string_view> shadow_cluster_name =","         getShadowCluster(shadow_policy, *downstream_headers_);","     if (!shadow_cluster_name.has_value()) {","+      if (shadow_policy.stats() != nullptr) {","+        shadow_policy.stats()->rq_no_cluster_.inc();","+      }","       continue;","     }","     const bool last_policy = (i == num_shadow_policies - 1);","@@ -988,10 +995,11 @@ bool Filter::continueDecodeHeaders(Http::RequestHeaderMap& headers, bool end_str","       // without waiting.","       Http::RequestMessagePtr request(new Http::RequestMessageImpl(std::move(shadow_headers)));","       config_->shadowWriter().shadow(std::string(shadow_cluster_name.value()), std::move(request),","-                                     options);","+                                     options, shadow_policy.stats());","     } else {","       Http::AsyncClient::OngoingRequest* shadow_stream = config_->shadowWriter().streamingShadow(","-          std::string(shadow_cluster_name.value()), std::move(shadow_headers), options);","+          std::string(shadow_cluster_name.value()), std::move(shadow_headers), options,","+          shadow_policy.stats());","       if (shadow_stream != nullptr) {","         ASSERT(std::find(shadow_streams_.begin(), shadow_streams_.end(), shadow_stream) ==","                shadow_streams_.end());"],"additions":11,"deletions":3,"truncated":false},{"path":"source/common/router/shadow_writer_impl.cc","lines":["@@ -3,9 +3,13 @@"," #include <chrono>"," #include <string>"," ","+#include \"envoy/router/router.h\"","+"," #include \"source/common/common/assert.h\"","+#include \"source/common/http/codes.h\""," #include \"source/common/http/header_utility.h\""," #include \"source/common/http/headers.h\"","+#include \"source/common/http/utility.h\""," "," #include \"absl/strings/str_join.h\""," ","@@ -29,25 +33,53 @@ std::string shadowAppendedHost(absl::string_view host) {"," } // namespace"," "," void ShadowWriterImpl::shadow(const std::string& cluster, Http::RequestMessagePtr&& request,","-                              const Http::AsyncClient::RequestOptions& options) {","+                              const Http::AsyncClient::RequestOptions& options,","+                              const ShadowPolicyStatsSharedPtr& stats) {","   const auto thread_local_cluster =","       getClusterAndPreprocessHeadersAndOptions(cluster, request->headers(), options);","   if (thread_local_cluster == nullptr) {","+    if (stats != nullptr) {","+      stats->rq_no_cluster_.inc();","+    }","+    return;","+  }","+  Http::AsyncClient& async_client = thread_local_cluster->httpAsyncClient();","+  if (stats == nullptr) {","+    // This is basically fire and forget. We don't handle cancelling.","+    async_client.send(std::move(request), *this, options);","     return;","   }","-  // This is basically fire and forget. We don't handle cancelling.","-  thread_local_cluster->httpAsyncClient().send(std::move(request), *this, options);","+  stats->rq_started_.inc();","+  auto* callbacks = new ShadowRequestCallbacks(stats, async_client.dispatcher());","+  if (async_client.send(std::move(request), *callbacks, options) == nullptr) {","+    callbacks->onStartFailed();","+  }"," }"," "," Http::AsyncClient::OngoingRequest*"," ShadowWriterImpl::streamingShadow(const std::string& cluster, Http::RequestHeaderMapPtr&& headers,","-                                  const Http::AsyncClient::RequestOptions& options) {","+                                  const Http::AsyncClient::RequestOptions& options,","+                                  const ShadowPolicyStatsSharedPtr& stats) {","   const auto thread_local_cluster =","       getClusterAndPreprocessHeadersAndOptions(cluster, *headers, options);","   if (thread_local_cluster == nullptr) {","+    if (stats != nullptr) {","+      stats->rq_no_cluster_.inc();","+    }","     return nullptr;","   }","-  return thread_local_cluster->httpAsyncClient().startRequest(std::move(headers), *this, options);","+  Http::AsyncClient& async_client = thread_local_cluster->httpAsyncClient();","+  if (stats == nullptr) {","+    return async_client.startRequest(std::move(headers), *this, options);","+  }","+  stats->rq_started_.inc();","+  auto* callbacks = new ShadowRequestCallbacks(stats, async_client.dispatcher());","+  Http::AsyncClient::OngoingRequest* request =","+      async_client.startRequest(std::move(headers), *callbacks, options);","+  if (request == nullptr) {","+    callbacks->onStartFailed();","+  }","+  return request;"," }"," "," Upstream::ThreadLocalCluster* ShadowWriterImpl::getClusterAndPreprocessHeadersAndOptions(","@@ -55,7 +87,6 @@ Upstream::ThreadLocalCluster* ShadowWriterImpl::getClusterAndPreprocessHeadersAn","     const Http::AsyncClient::RequestOptions& options) {","   // It's possible that the cluster specified in the route configuration no longer exists due","   // to a CDS removal. Check that it still exists before shadowing.","-  // TODO(mattklein123): Optimally we would have a stat but for now just fix the crashing issue.","   const auto thread_local_cluster = cm_.getThreadLocalCluster(cluster);","   if (thread_local_cluster == nullptr) {","     ENVOY_LOG(debug, \"shadow cluster '{}' does not exist\", cluster);","@@ -71,5 +102,46 @@ Upstream::ThreadLocalCluster* ShadowWriterImpl::getClusterAndPreprocessHeadersAn","   return thread_local_cluster;"," }"," ","+ShadowRequestCallbacks::~ShadowRequestCallbacks() {","+  if (!outcome_recorded_) {","+    stats_->rq_cancelled_.inc();","+  }","+}","+","+void ShadowRequestCallbacks::onSuccess(const Http::AsyncClient::Request&,","+                                       Http::ResponseMessagePtr&& response) {","+  outcome_recorded_ = true;","+  const std::optional<uint64_t> status =","+      Http::Utility::getResponseStatusOrNullopt(response->headers());","+  if (status.has_value() && Http::CodeUtility::is2xx(status.value())) {","+    stats_->rq_success_.inc();","+  } else {","+    stats_->rq_failure_.inc();","+  }","+}","+","+void ShadowRequestCallbacks::onFailure(const Http::AsyncClient::Request&,","+                                       Http::AsyncClient::FailureReason) {","+  outcome_recorded_ = true;","+  stats_->rq_failure_.inc();","+}","+","+void ShadowRequestCallbacks::onBeforeFinalizeUpstreamSpan(Envoy::Tracing::Span&,","+                                                          const Http::ResponseHeaderMap*) {","+  if (!finalized_) {","+    finalized_ = true;","+    dispatcher_.deferredDelete(Event::DeferredDeletablePtr{this});","+  }","+}","+","+void ShadowRequestCallbacks::onStartFailed() {","+  if (finalized_) {","+    return;","+  }","+  outcome_recorded_ = true;","+  stats_->rq_failure_.inc();","+  delete this;","+}","+"," } // namespace Router"," } // namespace Envoy"],"additions":78,"deletions":6,"truncated":false},{"path":"source/common/router/shadow_writer_impl.h","lines":["@@ -3,6 +3,8 @@"," #include <chrono>"," #include <string>"," ","+#include \"envoy/event/deferred_deletable.h\"","+#include \"envoy/event/dispatcher.h\""," #include \"envoy/router/shadow_writer.h\""," #include \"envoy/upstream/cluster_manager.h\""," ","@@ -21,11 +23,13 @@ class ShadowWriterImpl : Logger::Loggable<Logger::Id::router>,"," ","   // Router::ShadowWriter","   void shadow(const std::string& cluster, Http::RequestMessagePtr&& request,","-              const Http::AsyncClient::RequestOptions& options) override;","+              const Http::AsyncClient::RequestOptions& options,","+              const ShadowPolicyStatsSharedPtr& stats) override;"," ","   Http::AsyncClient::OngoingRequest*","   streamingShadow(const std::string& cluster, Http::RequestHeaderMapPtr&& headers,","-                  const Http::AsyncClient::RequestOptions& options) override;","+                  const Http::AsyncClient::RequestOptions& options,","+                  const ShadowPolicyStatsSharedPtr& stats) override;"," ","   // Http::AsyncClient::Callbacks","   void onSuccess(const Http::AsyncClient::Request&, Http::ResponseMessagePtr&&) override {}","@@ -41,5 +45,40 @@ class ShadowWriterImpl : Logger::Loggable<Logger::Id::router>,","   Upstream::ClusterManager& cm_;"," };"," ","+// TODO(wdauchy): the self-deletion relies on the async client calling","+// onBeforeFinalizeUpstreamSpan() exactly once per request, so a change in that behavior could leak","+// this object. Let the async client own the callbacks (e.g. via RequestOptions), or support","+// multiple destructor callbacks on Request, then remove the self-deletion.","+/**","+ * Async client callbacks of one mirror request of a policy with stats. They record how the mirror","+ * ended. The async client always calls onBeforeFinalizeUpstreamSpan() once when the request ends,","+ * before onSuccess() or onFailure() and also when the request is cancelled, so it schedules the","+ * deletion of this object. A request deleted without onSuccess() or onFailure() was cancelled.","+ */","+class ShadowRequestCallbacks : public Http::AsyncClient::Callbacks,","+                               public Event::DeferredDeletable {","+public:","+  ShadowRequestCallbacks(ShadowPolicyStatsSharedPtr stats, Event::Dispatcher& dispatcher)","+      : stats_(std::move(stats)), dispatcher_(dispatcher) {}","+  ~ShadowRequestCallbacks() override;","+","+  // Http::AsyncClient::Callbacks","+  void onSuccess(const Http::AsyncClient::Request&, Http::ResponseMessagePtr&& response) override;","+  void onFailure(const Http::AsyncClient::Request&, Http::AsyncClient::FailureReason) override;","+  void onBeforeFinalizeUpstreamSpan(Envoy::Tracing::Span&, const Http::ResponseHeaderMap*) override;","+","+  /**","+   * Records a failure and deletes the callbacks if the async client did not take ownership of","+   * the request, which happens when the request cannot be created.","+   */","+  void onStartFailed();","+","+private:","+  const ShadowPolicyStatsSharedPtr stats_;","+  Event::Dispatcher& dispatcher_;","+  bool finalized_{};","+  bool outcome_recorded_{};","+};","+"," } // namespace Router"," } // namespace Envoy"],"additions":41,"deletions":2,"truncated":false},{"path":"test/common/router/BUILD","lines":["@@ -597,6 +597,9 @@ envoy_cc_test(","         \"//source/common/http:headers_lib\",","         \"//source/common/http:message_lib\",","         \"//source/common/router:shadow_writer_lib\",","+        \"//source/common/stats:isolated_store_lib\",","+        \"//test/mocks/http:http_mocks\",","+        \"//test/mocks/tracing:tracing_mocks\",","         \"//test/mocks/upstream:cluster_manager_mocks\",","     ],"," )"],"additions":3,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"test/common/router/config_impl_test.cc","lines":["@@ -5010,6 +5010,50 @@ TEST_F(RouteMatcherTest, RequestMirrorPoliciesClusterHeader) {","   EXPECT_EQ(\"foo\", bar_shadow_policies[0]->runtimeKey());"," }"," ","+TEST_F(RouteMatcherTest, RequestMirrorPoliciesStatPrefix) {","+  const std::string yaml = R\"EOF(","+virtual_hosts:","+- name: www2","+  domains:","+  - www.lyft.com","+  routes:","+  - match:","+      prefix: \"/foo\"","+    route:","+      request_mirror_policies:","+        - cluster: some_cluster","+          stat_prefix: foo_mirror","+        - cluster: some_cluster","+      cluster: www2","+  )EOF\";","+","+  factory_context_.cluster_manager_.initializeClusters({\"www2\", \"some_cluster\"}, {});","+  ShadowPolicyStatsSharedPtr stats;","+  {","+    TestConfigImpl config(parseRouteConfigurationFromYaml(yaml), factory_context_, true,","+                          creation_status_);","+    const auto& shadow_policies =","+        config.route(genHeaders(\"www.lyft.com\", \"/foo\", \"GET\"), 0)->routeEntry()->shadowPolicies();","+    ASSERT_EQ(2, shadow_policies.size());","+    EXPECT_EQ(nullptr, s